    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can confirm the correct property from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to help responders locate the turn-in during low-visibility or nighttime conditions.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along both sides of the driveway so emergency vehicles can travel its full length without obstruction.\n• Maintain a minimum vertical clearance along the driveway to allow fire apparatus and ambulances to pass without branches contacting the vehicle.\n• Clear a turnaround area near the residence large enough for a fire engine or ambulance to reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Mark or communicate the turnaround location to arriving units so drivers do not commit to a dead end without a planned exit.\n• Keep the area around the detached structure clear of dense vegetation so responders can reach and move around it without obstruction.\n• Confirm that perimeter fencing has at least one gate accessible from the driveway and that the gate can be opened quickly without a key or combination.\n• Keep that gate unlocked or secured with a combination known to local fire and EMS, or install a Knox-compatible lock.\n• Post a simple site map at the driveway entrance showing the location of the main residence, detached structure, and any gates, so arriving responders can"
