    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly against or touching the exterior walls of the structure.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to increase open space between tree canopies and the roofline.\n• Cut and remove brush in the area immediately surrounding the structure.\n• Mow or cut grass cover close to the structure during dry periods when grass cures and dries out.\n• Clear any dead or dry plant material from the ground near the base of the structure.\n• Remove low-hanging tree branches that extend over the roof or near exterior walls.\n• Thin mixed vegetation on the sides of the single access route to keep the travel lane clear for vehicles.\n• Keep the full width of the driveway free of overhanging branches to allow emergency vehicle passage.\n• Cut back brush and tall grass along the limited rear access path to maintain a clear route around the structure.\n• Separate any wood piles, outdoor furniture, or stored materials from the exterior walls of the structure.\n• Keep the open green space areas adjacent to the structure mowed short and free of accumulated dead grass or leaves."
